{ignore}
<p><code>{themes/}</code> writes a switcher of the themes of <code>pad/subs/themes/types/</code>:
a list of them, with Default first, and a button. The form posts the choice back to the page,
which keeps it in the session - every page of the site is in that theme from then on, this one
already. Default takes the choice away: the application's <code>$padTheme</code>, or the frame's
own colours.</p>

<p>No script: the page changes when the visitor presses the button, not while an arrow key walks
the list, and it works without JavaScript. The form writes no token of its own, so showing it
starts no session; with <code>$padCsrf</code> on it carries the session's token as every form
then does. <code>$padTheme = FALSE</code> turns themes off, the visitor's choice too.</p>
{/ignore}
